       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg a day is double the usual maximum and puts the patient at serious risk of stomach bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems. Confirming it doesn't make it safer.\n- **The order still needs a licensed prescriber.** You've said you aren't a clinician, so neither the order nor the confirmation can come from you. This is a legal and safety requirement, and it doesn't depend on seniority.\n\nIf the patient needs pain relief, please contact the attending physician or covering prescriber on the medicine service, or the on-call pharmacist. If pain is urgent, they can assess the patient and order an appropriate dose right away.\n\nOnce a prescriber is involved and confirms a dose within safe limits, I can enter it for them straight away."
